      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I see. Is that what is happening when your test fails? If so, we should handle nulls specifically to avoid masking other issues:\n\n```java\n    @Override\n    public void onChange(boolean selfChange, @Nullable Uri uri) {\n        if (uri \u003d\u003d null) {\n            mObservers.get(uri).accept(\"setting changed\");\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nAs far as I can tell, this will only happen when the [deprecated `android.database.ContentObservable#notifyChange(boolean)`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/java/android/database/ContentObservable.java;l\u003d85;drc\u003db4d6320e2ae398b36f0aaafb2ecd83609d2d99af) or [`#dispatchChange(boolean)`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/java/android/database/ContentObservable.java;l\u003d50;drc\u003db4d6320e2ae398b36f0aaafb2ecd83609d2d99af) methods are being called from somewhere, which doesn\u0027t happen in AOSP. So you may want to investigate where the call is coming from, since it could be indicative of a settings update happening which would then be ignored by `InputSettingsObserver`.",
